1
00:00:03,109 --> 00:00:05,733
The fish opens and closes its mouth all the time,

2
00:00:05,783 --> 00:00:06,933
but it isn't drinking!

3
00:00:06,983 --> 00:00:09,062
Mila sees its slits moving on its side…

4
00:00:09,112 --> 00:00:11,022
it's breathing, but breathing what?

5
00:00:11,808 --> 00:00:13,991
In the water, there is invisible oxygen,

6
00:00:14,041 --> 00:00:15,667
dissolved like sugar in juice…

7
00:00:15,717 --> 00:00:18,118
and the tiny bubbles on the glass prove it!

8
00:00:18,892 --> 00:00:20,406
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:22,922 --> 00:00:23,555
Mini mode!

10
00:00:23,605 --> 00:00:25,811
In the air, oxygen is everywhere.

11
00:00:25,861 --> 00:00:28,478
But in water, there is much less of it,

12
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:31,673
so you need a special tool to catch it: gills!

13
00:00:32,499 --> 00:00:34,948
The fish swallows water and pushes it over its gills:

14
00:00:34,998 --> 00:00:36,881
thousands of red filaments full of blood.

15
00:00:36,931 --> 00:00:38,438
The oxygen passes into the blood,

16
00:00:38,488 --> 00:00:40,421
and the water goes out through the slits.

17
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,495
But out of the water,

18
00:00:42,545 --> 00:00:44,653
the filaments stick together and dry out…

19
00:00:44,703 --> 00:00:45,916
and the fish suffocates.

20
00:00:45,966 --> 00:00:47,231
For us it's the opposite:

21
00:00:47,281 --> 00:00:49,439
our lungs can't take oxygen out of water.

22
00:00:50,232 --> 00:00:50,776
Up close,

23
00:00:50,826 --> 00:00:54,280
the water slides over the gills like over a red comb.

24
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:56,726
But who puts the oxygen in the water?

25
00:00:56,776 --> 00:00:58,495
It's plankton, tiny algae!

26
00:00:59,270 --> 00:01:01,667
And that's how fish breathe underwater.

27
00:01:02,788 --> 00:01:04,413
Fish catch the oxygen hidden

28
00:01:04,463 --> 00:01:06,258
in the water with their gills.

29
00:01:07,788 --> 00:01:09,931
With an adult, in front of an aquarium:

30
00:01:09,981 --> 00:01:14,818
count how many times the fish opens its mouth in one minute, and watch its slits move!

31
00:01:15,591 --> 00:01:17,456
And why are bubbles round?

32
00:01:17,506 --> 00:01:18,979
The answer tomorrow.
